WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.070
A function machine: f
of x equals one over x.

2
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:06.890
Feed in two, and out comes a half.

3
00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.790
Now feed that half back in.

4
00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:10.330
Out comes two again.

5
00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:13.440
Try another machine: five minus x.

6
00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:17.160
Two goes to three, and three
goes straight back to two.

7
00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:19.220
Doing it twice undoes it.

8
00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:21.790
Each function is its own inverse.

9
00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:23.770
So what must its graph look like?

10
00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:26.290
Symmetric somehow, but how?

11
00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:32.650
In this mission, you'll see that f of f
of x equals x means f inverse is f itself:

12
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.030
the function is self-inverse.

13
00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:40.010
You'll also meet even and odd functions,
two other kinds of symmetry in a graph.

14
00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:44.430
Your mission: decide what a self-inverse
function's graph must look like.
